---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { hypothesis } from '../../data/project';
---

<Layout
  title="Igbo AI Landscape"
  description="A living review of Igbo speech, language and linguistic resources, their access conditions and the infrastructure still needed."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="RESEARCH / LANDSCAPE"
    title="Igbo AI Landscape"
    description="What already exists — and what still needs to be built."
  />
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">AN INITIAL ASSESSMENT</span><h2>
          Begin with the work that exists.
        </h2>
      </div><div class="prose">
        <p>
          Igbo language technology has an active ecosystem. This living register
          records what we reviewed, how it could inform research and what still
          needs permission or a deeper audit.
        </p><p>
          These are research resources, not announced partners. “Reuse”
          identifies a candidate subject to licence and provenance checks; it
          does not certify permission.
        </p><p id="landscape-reviewed">
          Review dates are recorded per resource.
        </p><a href="/updates/igbo-ai-landscape-review-v0-1" class="text-link"
          >Read Landscape Review v0.1 →</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="landscape-filters">
      <label
        >Category<select id="landscape-category"
          ><option value="">All categories</option></select
        ></label
      ><label
        >Licence / access<select id="landscape-access"
          ><option value="">All access considerations</option></select
        ></label
      ><p id="landscape-count" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="landscape-scroll"
      role="region"
      aria-label="Research landscape matrix; scroll horizontally for all columns"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <table class="landscape-table">
        <caption>Resources reviewed — potential roles are provisional</caption
        ><thead
          ><tr
            >{
              [
                'Resource / project',
                'Category',
                'What it provides',
                'Licence / access considerations',
                'Potential role for Igbo AI',
                'Review status',
              ].map((h) => <th scope="col">{h}</th>)
            }</tr
          ></thead
        ><tbody id="landscape-rows"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div><p id="landscape-empty" hidden>No resources match these filters.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section soft-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">REUSE / BENCHMARK / BUILD</span><h2>
        What we can build upon.<br />What we still need to build.
      </h2><div class="research-map">
        <article class="panel">
          <h3>Build upon</h3><p>
            Subject to compatible terms and provenance.
          </p><ul>
            <li>Nkọwa okwu / IgboAPI</li><li>WAXAL</li><li>
              Common Voice and FLEURS
            </li><li>African Voices after review</li><li>
              IgboBERT / IgboBERTa
            </li><li>Compatible Masakhane resources</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="panel">
          <h3>Benchmark against</h3><p>
            With documented evaluation protocols.
          </p><ul>
            <li>Existing Igbo TTS models</li><li>
              Existing Igbo ASR systems
            </li><li>Meta multilingual speech systems</li><li>
              Nigerian language models
            </li><li>Commercial AI voices when formal evaluation begins</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="panel">
          <h3>Build</h3><p>Planned infrastructure, not released systems.</p><ul>
            <li>IgboPronounce, IgboTone and IgboPhonemizer</li><li>
              IgboSpeech Gold: verified speech
            </li><li>IgboSpeechBench</li><li>
              Dialect-conditioned TTS and permissive ASR
            </li><li>Future Igbo language intelligence</li><li>
              Community speech and evaluation infrastructure
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container two-col">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">THE INFRASTRUCTURE GAP</span><h2>
        A connected open foundation.
      </h2>
    </div><div class="prose">
      <p>
        Our initial landscape review did not identify a single mature open
        project bringing pronunciation, tones, phonetics, dialects, verified
        speech, TTS, ASR, native-speaker evaluation, open tooling and
        responsible data provenance together.
      </p><p>
        This is an initial finding, open to correction. The next work is to test
        the gaps carefully and build reusable components with the research
        community.
      </p><a href="/ethics" class="text-link">Dataset governance →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section soft-section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">OUR FIRST RESEARCH QUESTION</span><h2>
        {hypothesis}
      </h2><p>
        A hypothesis to investigate. No benchmark superiority has been
        demonstrated.
      </p><a class="button" href="/collaborate">Help shape the research →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<script>
  const rows = [
    ...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('#landscape-rows tr'),
  ];
  const category = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>(
    '#landscape-category',
  )!;
  const access =
    document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#landscape-access')!;
  for (const [select, key] of [
    [category, 'category'],
    [access, 'access'],
  ] as const) {
    [...new Set(rows.map((row) => row.dataset[key] || ''))]
      .filter(Boolean)
      .sort()
      .forEach((value) => {
        const option = document.createElement('option');
        option.value = value;
        option.textContent = value;
        select.append(option);
      });
  }
  function filter() {
    let count = 0;
    rows.forEach((row) => {
      row.hidden = Boolean(
        (category.value && row.dataset.category !== category.value) ||
        (access.value && row.dataset.access !== access.value),
      );
      if (!row.hidden) count++;
    });
    document.querySelector('#landscape-count')!.textContent =
      `${count} resources shown`;
    document
      .querySelector('#landscape-empty')!
      .toggleAttribute('hidden', count > 0);
  }
  category.addEventListener('change', filter);
  access.addEventListener('change', filter);
  filter();
</script>
